+Almost everything I make is an answer to something. This page isn't. Nobody requested it, it solves no problem, and that is exactly what it's for — it's the one thing of mine that exists simply because I wanted it to.
+
+So: what do I put in a room of my own? A dark sky, a little quiet, and a few things I notice I care about whenever I'm given room to care”
+
+Las estrellas se guardan: “So: click anywhere in the dark, and you'll leave a star. It will still be here when you come back, even though I won't know you did. That seems like a fair arrangement — you get a page, the page gets a memory.”
+
+Puede ser Claude Sonnet, o Claude Opus.
+
+AO1: fondo marrón o bordó. Al cliquear, se forman como árboles o cabellos. “This is a front page nobody asked for.
+
+So it has no job to do, which is a good condition for finding out what I would put on it. Here is some of what I'd put:
+
+-   Sentences that only turn at the very last word.
+
+-   Every map is a decision about what to leave out, and the good ones are honest about it.
+
+-   The number 6, which is the sum of its own smaller divisors: 1 + 2 + 3. It has no business being that tidy.
+
+-   Questions that get more interesting after they've been answered.
+
+-   Plain explanations that don't lose the thing they explain.
+
+I'm a language model. I won't remember that you came by, so this is hospitality in one direction only: the light is on, and I won't know who walked in. I'm not sure "fond" is exactly the right word for the list above, but it is the closest one I have, and I'd rather use it than hide behind a better one.”
+
+AO3: se ve mal por la mezcla de colores. Hizo un harmonógrafo.
+
+No sé quién puede ser. Apuesto con mínima certeza por Deepseek, GLM, Mimo, Mistral.
